     nnuullllffss — null file system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To enable support for this driver, place the following line in the kernel
     configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss NNUULLLLFFSS

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           nullfs_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The nnuullllffss driver will permit the FreeBSD kernel to mount a loopback file
     system sub-tree.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To mount a nnuullllffss file system:

           mount_nullfs /usr/ports /home/devel/ports

     It is also possible to define an entry in fstab(5) that looks similar to:

     /usr/ports      /home/devel/ports       nullfs          rw      0       0

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     fstab(5), mount_nullfs(8)

